From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:29:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: drop the CHRE daemon for now

chre_daemon_msm never finishes init on this build: every fastrpc
remote_handle_open against the SLPI returns 0xfffffffb, so it logs
"Failed to send initial time sync message" / "failed to init the daemon"
and exits non-zero. init restarts it 33 times in one boot, counts the
5th bad exit before sys.boot_completed, and sets
sys.init.updatable_crashing -- and apexd answers that by reverting and
rebooting. Same boot-killing path as the camera provider in the previous
commit; both have to go for a boot to complete.

0021 dropped the HIDL context hub HAL and nothing replaced it, so no
framework client is left for CHRE. Stop packaging the daemon until the
DSP side is understood.

---
 device-lineage.mk | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device-lineage.mk b/device-lineage.mk
index 10a2fcb8..8888cd1d 100644
--- a/device-lineage.mk
+++ b/device-lineage.mk
@@ -65,9 +65,13 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 
 # Build necessary packages for vendor
 
-# CHRE
-PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-    chre_daemon_msm
+# CHRE. The daemon cannot reach the SLPI: every fastrpc remote_handle_open on the DSP fails, so
+# it logs "failed to init the daemon" and exits non-zero, 33 times per boot. init counts the 5th
+# exit before sys.boot_completed and sets sys.init.updatable_crashing, which makes apexd revert
+# and reboot. 0021 already dropped the context hub HAL, so nothing consumes CHRE anyway -- do not
+# ship the daemon until the DSP side works.
+#PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+#    chre_daemon_msm
 
 # Display
 $(call soong_config_set,qtidisplay,drmpp,true)
